import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Sources">
  <header class="masthead">
    <p class="kicker">फल · sources</p>
    <h1>The texts behind the reading</h1>
    <p class="sub">What is quoted, and what has been checked.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>Primary</h2>
    <p class="strap">the verses</p>
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        <strong>Phaladīpikā</strong> of Mantreśvara. Chapters 6, 7, 9, 10, 16, 19,
        22 and 26 are transcribed, ninety-one verses in all. The printed edition
        used for checking is Mantreśvara, <em>Phaladeepika</em>, adhyāyas I–XXVIII,
        translated by P. V. Subrahmanya Sastri, second edition, Munshiram Manoharlal,
        Delhi, 1950.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Bṛhat Parāśara Horā Śāstra</strong>, Vol I, translated by R. Santhanam.
        Used to cross-check the method, and for the dispute over the seventh lord in
        the fifth: the verse there reads favourably, while Santhanam's own notes
        record the opposite in practice. Both are kept.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Bṛhat Jātaka</strong> of Varāhamihira, translated by P. S. Sastri.
        Used for the nakṣatra material and for cross-checking aspects. Its Devanagari
        is corrupt in the available scan, so nothing is quoted from it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>What is not here</h2>
    <p class="strap">and why</p>
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        A twelve-domain panel of twenty-three rules was withdrawn. The first cited
        Phaladīpikā chapter 14 for a verse that is not in it — that chapter is
        रोगनिर्णयः, on diagnosing disease. One fabricated citation removes the reason
        to trust the other twenty-two, so the panel went rather than stand with a
        disclaimer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sāmudrika Śāstra was considered and set aside. It reads the body, not the
        birth moment, and has no place in a reading produced from birth data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
